msgid "tale.sea_bottle"
msgstr "A bottle of dark glass, its neck sealed with pitch. Inside, a strip of birch bark with letters burnt in with a needle: 'Whoever finds this, light the fire on Gull Skerry. We steered for it three days and never arrived; the fog ate the way. The boat is whole, the people are whole, the fish are few. If the fire is lit we will see it and come.' No signature. The Pomors said such letters are written not to be rescued but so that people remember what the beacons are for."

msgid "tale.puchinnik"
msgstr "The Deep One lives in the deep water of the Ter Coast and the Frozen Sea and comes out at night when the Mga lies on the water. Nobody calls it by name: say it and it swims up. First it circles, and the boat rocks without a wave. Then it grips the hull and the boat stands as if tied while it beats at the side. Strike it three times in a row and it lets go and draws off. It cannot bear fire: a torch in hand or a lantern at the bow keeps it at a distance. A harpoon reaches it from the deck and comes back on its line. It does not sink boats and does not touch the hold; it wants not cargo but fear."

